<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26096" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτορ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείρω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>piercing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέδαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					76
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φόβος</span>
			<i>thrilling</i> fear, ib.<i><span class="en">
				181
			</span></i> (lyr.); of sound, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Τυρσηνικὴ σάλπιγξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					567
				</span></i>
			: neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτορον φθέγγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.303e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναβοᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Gall.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>pierced, bored through,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδοῖν ἀκμαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1034
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
